      {
        "id": 92411,
        "name": "McBehrer",
        "username": "McBehrer",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/mcbehrer/{size}/1850_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-02-19T00:06:06.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>they get an additional power. Any time that phrasing is used -- may do ____ now -- it does not count towards the limit on how many you can do per turn. That's why you can chain together all 3 of Tachyon's Fleet of Foots, Hud Goggles, Pushing The Limits, Lightspeed Reflexes (play 2 cards now), Lightspeed Reflexes, and still be able to play 3 more cards before your play phase is up.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>The only exceptions that come to mind are</p><p>A.) Vengeance Blade's Impulsion Beam, which SPECIFICALLY limits each hero to 1 play and 1 power per turn, no matter what,</p><p>and</p><p>B.) The standing rule that you can only use EACH power once per turn. So unless you have a Gauge or Seg Fault or something in play already, you might want to give the power to someone else so you CAN do something during your power phase.</p>",
        "post_number": 2,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:18:20.711Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 0,
