      {
        "id": 92412,
        "name": "Ameena",
        "username": "Ameena",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ameena/{size}/1907_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-02-19T00:11:45.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>When you play a card that lets someone use a power and target yourself, you're still within your Play phase as you haven't yet finished resolving the card you just played - assuming there are no other instructions after the \"use a power now\" part of the card, said card will be resolved once your power's effect has finished. So were you to use such a card on a fully set up Adept, you might be waiting a while for it to finish ;). Anyway, once that's done, then it's your Power phase and you proceed with that as normal, and like McBehrer says, you still only get to use a specific instance of a power once per turn so if you used your played card on yourself to use a power in your Play phase, you won't be able to use that same power now it's your Power phase. Obviously, if you have two copies of a non-Limited power-granting card out and used one off the one-shot, you're free to use the second copy's power in your Power phase, though :).</p>",
        "post_number": 3,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:18:20.798Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 0,
