        "can_see_hidden_post": false,
        "can_wiki": false,
        "read": false,
        "user_title": null,
        "bookmarked": false,
        "raw": "<p>When you play a card that lets someone use a power and target yourself, you&#39;re still within your Play phase as you haven&#39;t yet finished resolving the card you just played - assuming there are no other instructions after the &quot;use a power now&quot; part of the card, said card will be resolved once your power&#39;s effect has finished. So were you to use such a card on a fully set up Adept, you might be waiting a while for it to finish ;). Anyway, once that&#39;s done, then it&#39;s your Power phase and you proceed with that as normal, and like McBehrer says, you still only get to use a specific instance of a power once per turn so if you used your played card on yourself to use a power in your Play phase, you won&#39;t be able to use that same power now it&#39;s your Power phase. Obviously, if you have two copies of a non-Limited power-granting card out and used one off the one-shot, you&#39;re free to use the second copy&#39;s power in your Power phase, though :).</p>",
