      {
        "id": 92413,
        "name": "Matchstickman",
        "username": "Matchstickman",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/matchstickman/{size}/1880_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-02-19T00:17:35.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>You don't ordinarily get to use \"one power\" in your power phase you get to use \"a power\". If something was limiting you to only 1 power each turn then Hasty Augmentation or Between the Lines would use up that 1 power limit for the turn, but there is no such limit in the game ordinarily and HA and BtL do not apply such a limit.</p><p>If played on their respective characters they could still use a power during their power phase, just not the same power that HA/BtL had let them use (that is to say, not the same power from the same card- the standard limit the game applied to all).</p>",
        "post_number": 4,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:18:20.904Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 0,
        "reads": 1,
        "readers_count": 0,
        "score": 0.2,
        "yours": false,
        "topic_id": 9580,
        "topic_slug": "one-hero-may-use-a-power-now",
        "display_username": "Matchstickman",
        "primary_group_name": "playtesters",
        "flair_name": "playtesters",
        "flair_url": "/uploads/default/original/1X/f46928191dbf93b4d0df24571543f49779579225.png",
        "flair_bg_color": "",
        "flair_color": "",
        "flair_group_id": 41,
        "badges_granted": [],
        "version": 1,
        "can_edit": false,
        "can_delete": false,
        "can_recover": false,
        "can_see_hidden_post": false,
        "can_wiki": false,
        "read": false,
        "user_title": null,
        "bookmarked": false,
        "raw": "<p>You don&#39;t ordinarily get to use &quot;one power&quot; in your power phase you get to use &quot;a power&quot;. If something was limiting you to only 1 power each turn then Hasty Augmentation or Between the Lines would use up that 1 power limit for the turn, but there is no such limit in the game ordinarily and HA and BtL do not apply such a limit.</p><p>If played on their respective characters they could still use a power during their power phase, just not the same power that HA/BtL had let them use (that is to say, not the same power from the same card- the standard limit the game applied to all).</p>",
        "actions_summary": [
