      {
        "id": 92414,
        "name": "Envisioner",
        "username": "Envisioner",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/e/9de053/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2014-02-19T19:08:23.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>You get to use one Power right then and there, and you may use another one during your power phase as normal, but you cannot use the same Power both times (from your character card, or from one particular Ongoing or Equipment card in play - a second copy of the same card is a separate Power even though it does the same thing).&nbsp; Each Power may be used no more than once per turn, and the normal number of powers you can use in a turn is 1; Hasty Augmentation grants another 1 to that total that turn.&nbsp; If you get a power usage when it isn't your turn, however, you can use the same Power you used on your last turn.</p><p>Note also the difference between card effects which tell you to skip your power phase (does not prevent using Hasty Augmentation to at least get one power that turn) and ones which tell you that you can't use Powers (does prevent it).</p>",
        "post_number": 5,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:18:20.987Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
